; expect 42
; A `match` inside a `while` body, and a nested constructor pattern
; over a parameterised scrutinee - two shapes one line each, both of
; which the compiler refused or miscompiled until 2026-08-21.
;
; `bodyHasMatch` decides whether a function gets the one-word scratch
; cell every `match` merges through. A `while`'s second word is its
; body VECTOR, and the walk handed it to the node case, which read a
; Vec header as a tag and answered 0: no scratch, and `opt` refused
; the undefined `%__scr.h` as AX4003 - in the program, for a loop
; that matched. `walk` below is that loop.
;
; `deep` is the exhaustiveness half. The matrix spliced a
; constructor's DECLARED field types into the inner column, so over
; `(Option (Option Int))` the inner column was the declaration's `a`
; - enumerable by nothing but a binder - and the three arms that
; cover every value were AX3005 "some values are not covered". The
; column's own arguments are substituted now (`matCtorsExh`), and
; the program compiles.
;
; 30 + 12 = 42.
(data MyList (a) (MNil) (MCons a (MyList a)))
(:: walk (-> (MyList Int) Int))
(fn (walk l)
  (let ((mut cur l) (mut acc 0) (mut go 1))
    {
      (while (== go 1)
        (match cur
          ((MCons h t) { (set acc (+ acc h)) (set cur t) })
          ((MNil) (set go 0))))
      acc
    }))
(:: deep (-> (Option (Option Int)) Int))
(fn (deep o)
  (match o
    ((Some (Some x)) (+ x 1))
    ((Some (None)) 1)
    ((None) 0)))
(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (+ (walk (MCons 10 (MCons 20 MNil)))
     (deep (Some (Some 11)))))
